  "id": "Compound::DB01181 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Ifosfamide is likely to interact with Cyp2c9 through a series of molecular and enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests that Ifosfamide binds to Cyp2c18 or Cyp2c8, which are both involved in arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity or oxidoreductase activity, respectively. These activities are ultimately participated by Cyp2c9, indicating a potential functional link between Ifosfamide and the enzyme. The shared involvement of Cyp2c9 in these metabolic processes implies that Ifosfamide may influence the activity of Cyp2c9 through its binding to these enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Ifosfamide could modulate Cyp2c9 function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
